contrib: no librist on QNX.

librist is new among the contribs of 3.0.24 (3.0.21 had none) and serves
the RIST access/output modules only. On QNX it does not build as it is:
no <sys/endian.h> (QNX has the functions in <net/netbyte.h>); the
contribs' Meson cross file names the system 'linux', so it compiles
src/tun_linux.c, which is empty off Linux (an error under its
-pedantic-errors) while rist.c still calls rist_tun_read/rist_tun_write;
and its bundled cJSON references glibc's __isinf. Leave it out on QNX:
VLC's configure then builds without the RIST modules.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [QNX build choice]

diff --git a/contrib/src/librist/rules.mak b/contrib/src/librist/rules.mak
index d0e3648..1645dbe 100644
--- a/contrib/src/librist/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/librist/rules.mak
@@ -4,8 +4,13 @@ LIBRIST_VERSION := v0.2.20
 LIBRIST_URL := $(VIDEOLAN_GIT)/rist/librist/-/archive/$(LIBRIST_VERSION)/librist-$(LIBRIST_VERSION).tar.gz
 
 ifdef BUILD_NETWORK
+# not on QNX: librist takes Linux's tun device and endian header as given
+# (src/tun_linux.c through the cross file's system = 'linux'), and its
+# bundled cJSON calls glibc's __isinf; VLC builds without its RIST module
+ifndef HAVE_QNX
 PKGS += librist
 endif
+endif
 
 DEPS_librist =
 ifdef HAVE_WIN32
